Sun Nov  1 15:21:08 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.0.0:
  * Intentional break: uuid6, uuid7 and uuid8 follow the
    signatures Python 3.14 added to the standard library;
    the legacy 0.x signatures are removed.
  * uuid6(node, clock_seq), uuid7(nanoseconds=...),
    uuid8(a, b, c); uuid1, uuid3, uuid4, uuid5 and the UUID
    type are unchanged.
  * UUID(..., version=N) now sets the RFC 4122 variant.
  * Raise the Python floor to 3.10.
  * Refresh the vendored Rust crates (pyo3 0.29, uuid 1.26,
    rand 0.10).

